From: NSS integration <nss@local>
Subject: [PATCH] frontends: match slow-path QoS priority to packet direction

NSS CREATE programs flow_qos_tag and return_qos_tag separately. The common
IPv4 and IPv6 host paths nevertheless copy flow_qos_tag into every skb,
including replies. A connection whose classifier returns distinct tags can
therefore change priority when packets transition between host and firmware.

Use the sender already resolved against the connection's FROM address to
select the same direction that NSS CREATE uses. Preserve the complete tag;
this changes no rate, queue limit, classifier result or acceleration policy.

--- a/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv4.c
+++ b/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv4.c
@@ -1357,10 +1357,10 @@ unsigned int ecm_ported_ipv4_process(struct net_device *out_dev,
 	ecm_db_connection_data_totals_update(ci, (sender == ECM_TRACKER_SENDER_TYPE_SRC)? true : false, skb->len, 1);
 
 	/*
-	 * Assign qos tag
-	 * GGG TODO Should we use sender to identify whether to use flow or return qos tag?
+	 * Match the flow/return QoS tags programmed into the accelerated rule.
 	 */
-	skb->priority = prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag;
+	skb->priority = (sender == ECM_TRACKER_SENDER_TYPE_SRC) ?
+		prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag : prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag;
 	DEBUG_TRACE("%px: skb priority: %u\n", ci, skb->priority);
 
 	/*
--- a/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv6.c
+++ b/frontends/cmn/ecm_ported_ipv6.c
@@ -1377,10 +1377,10 @@ unsigned int ecm_ported_ipv6_process(struct net_device *out_dev,
 	ecm_db_connection_data_totals_update(ci, (sender == ECM_TRACKER_SENDER_TYPE_SRC)? true : false, skb->len, 1);
 
 	/*
-	 * Assign qos tag
-	 * GGG TODO Should we use sender to identify whether to use flow or return qos tag?
+	 * Match the flow/return QoS tags programmed into the accelerated rule.
 	 */
-	skb->priority = prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag;
+	skb->priority = (sender == ECM_TRACKER_SENDER_TYPE_SRC) ?
+		prevalent_pr.flow_qos_tag : prevalent_pr.return_qos_tag;
 	DEBUG_TRACE("%px: skb priority: %u\n", ci, skb->priority);
 
